{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Every weapon formed.</b> That is formed against you, for it will not succeed, but will break — here יוֹצֵר is from the binyan whose verbal noun is not called on the pattern of יוֹסֵר (Leviticus 4:35):" "<b>And every tongue, etc.</b> Now this is the interpretation of 'every weapon':" "<b>You shall condemn.</b> The meaning: the nations will believe in the Torah, and Israel will see the wickedness of their religions." "<b>This is the heritage of the servants of YHWH.</b> From HaShem — on account of the Torah, or on account of the land of the deer:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 54, :notes {0 "The contrast is between יוֹצֵר (pausal/participle-like form from יצר II, 'to form, fashion') and the pattern יוֹסֵר (po'el); Ibn Ezra's point is that here the form does not carry the expected morphological pattern."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:37.612133934Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}